  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nAt least partly cloudy skies will persist as an upper trough pivots \nover the area today. While the bulk of the area should remain dry, \nsome drizzle could materialize over the northeast mountains this \nmorning. Skies will gradually clear as the trough departs to the \nnortheast and high pressure builds in from the southwest later today \nand tonight. \n\nNortheast flow will keep temperatures cooler than normal today, with \nhighs expected to stay in the 50s in the lowlands and mid 30s to \nupper 40s in the mountains. Lows will then descend into the 20s to \n30s overnight; therefore, a Freeze Warning has been issued for all \ncounties where the growing season has yet to end (roughly along and \nsouth of the I-64 corridor) from midnight tonight through 10 AM \nSunday morning.\n\nDry conditions are generally expected to prevail through the middle \nof next week, while temperatures moderate toward normal. Nights will \nremain chilly, facilitating additional opportunities for early \nmorning frost.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nPrecipitation chances return to the area by Thursday and linger\nthrough the end of the week as an upper-level trough and low \nmigrate east across the forecast area. \n\nThis system is projected to bring much colder air down into the \nMiddle Ohio Valley, which could allow rain to transition to snow \nalong the mountains.",
